        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Otto von Bismarck\n- Places: Poland, rural Poland\n- Governments: totalitarian German government\n- Events: colonization of Poland by German settlers\n- Works: The Outpost\n- Concepts: plight of rural Poland\n\nFacts:\n- Otto von Bismarck held the royal titles Prince of Bismarck and Duke of Lauenburg.\n- A totalitarian German government backed the colonization of Poland by German settlers.\n- The colonization of Poland by German settlers was one of the factors that led to the plight of rural Poland.\n- The novel The Outpost focused on the plight of rural Poland.",
